[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one issue, one fix. Read by cause instead of by
subject line, its reports are three problems. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: `parser` is
fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`), `hint` is won't fix because booking-v3's form is
retired. The one-day moves are fixed by neither, and stay open.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket. The table is the desk's view of #4471,
computed from its reports when this page renders.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} {filed} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: the parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant in #4471 writes the day first, so
day and month come out swapped: "Our 7 April reminder went out on 4 July." This is the bug #4471
names. Fixed on 5 October.

**`hint`: booking-v3's form tells people to type month first.** Its date field says `MM/DD/YYYY`,
but the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. People type what the hint says, and the
date is stored swapped. The parser fix does not touch this: only form bookings on booking-v3 hit
it. Won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired, and its hint with it.

**One-day moves: dates land one day off** ([its own ticket]({shiftTicket})). Not swapped:
"Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." That points at time zones, not at
date order. The desk has these in its one-day-move notes, and the view files them under `parser`
by tenant: they are the footnote under the table, counted inside the `parser` row. The parser fix
will not close them. One reporter says they have stopped reporting these, so the count is a floor.

## Why one ticket hid them

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. All three
  problems arrive as "wrong day on the invite", so subject matching put them in one ticket.
- Intake tags each report from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant. The `tagged as`
  column shows how far the tags are from the causes.
- The export pages overlap: some reports appear twice. Counts here are by report id.

## For the desk

#4471 is closed, but the one-day moves are not: follow them on [their ticket]({shiftTicket}). When
a report is about a date, check the tenant's booking form and whether the date is swapped or one
day off before you merge it.

